Z||000000||Stoic||04-06-2001||08:50 PM||||This may be a dumb question, and probably asked before, but here goes.  I want to put a 6 cyl. (new/crate engine)  where my 4cyl is now (auto trans.).  Will pretty much any 6 cyl pop in?  In particular, I am considering something along the lines of a grand prix GTP engine or anything capable of equal performance.  Will the trans bolt up to that, any major modifications besides computer, wireing harness, etc.?   <P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||04-07-2001||12:02 AM||||Yes. it's been asked. allot of the details are available thru search system.<P>You need a front wheel drive V6 or you'll go nuts doing it.<P>you need all the crap that goes with the motor in question. Only certain versions of V6 work with the V6 fiero electrical. Your best bet is stay with those. Other wise all bets are off and you'll have to fabricate the entire harness for them.||||reg||1
